## Changes

- **`lib/load-color-data.ts`**: When computing `color` for each base color group, prefer the parsed hex from `colorHexMap` over the static default:
  1. Check `colorHexMap` for the canonical color name (e.g. `"sininen"` for the `sininen` base)
  2. Fall back to the first variant in the group that has an entry in `colorHexMap`
  3. Fall back to `getDefaultHex(baseColor)` if no data-derived hex exists

```ts
let hexFromData = colorHexMap.get(mainColorName);
if (hexFromData === undefined) {
  for (const variant of variantArray) {
    const variantHex = colorHexMap.get(variant);
    if (variantHex !== undefined) {
      hexFromData = variantHex;
      break;
    }
  }
}
const hex = hexFromData ?? getDefaultHex(baseColor);
```

